WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.942
This query combines Modules 11 and 12.

00:00:02.942 --> 00:00:06.102
The view owns the stable patient-admission interface.

00:00:06.102 --> 00:00:10.062
The CTEs own report-specific sequence and readmission logic.

00:00:10.062 --> 00:00:13.122
LAG calculates the previous discharge.

00:00:13.122 --> 00:00:17.097
The final threshold checks whether the gap is within thirty days.

00:00:17.097 --> 00:00:24.437
This separation keeps the stable data interface reusable while allowing reports to define their own analytical

00:00:24.437 --> 00:00:29.517
rules. A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:35.937
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:35.937 --> 00:00:41.955
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
